§§ `Everyone: reporting (ss 3, 17, 18)`

-- s 3: Graham's death at home is a Western Australian death; it is not reportable while expected, natural and certified; a
-- fall (injury), a lock-up (held in care) and no certificate (limb (i)) make it reportable.
#ASSERT `Is this death a Western Australian death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `nothing of these` `no exception` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this death a Western Australian death` `as a doctor present` `in WA, body here` TRUE `another limb` `no exception` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this death a Western Australian death` `as someone else who knows` `in WA, body here` FALSE `held in care` `no exception` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is this a Western Australian death` `Graham, lock-up`)
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `nothing of these` `no exception` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `another limb` `no exception` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as family` `in WA, body here` FALSE `nothing of these` `no exception` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is this a reportable death` `Graham, uncertified`)
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as a doctor present` `in WA, body here` FALSE `nothing of these` `no exception` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as someone else who knows` `in WA, body here` FALSE `held in care` `no exception` EQUALS yes

-- s 17(1): anyone aware, unless they reasonably believe it already reported; s 17(3): the doctor present, also where they
-- cannot determine the cause or think it suspicious; s 17(4): not once another doctor present has reported.
