§§ `The family: the investigation, the inquest, the next of kin, the post mortem and the body`

#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `nothing of these` `no exception` `no such direction` FALSE EQUALS `the investigation` `no: it is not a reportable death, so the coroner has no jurisdiction (s 19(1))`
#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `only unexpected` `no exception` `no such direction` TRUE EQUALS `the investigation` `the coroner need not investigate: natural causes, reportable only because unexpected (s 19A)`
#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` FALSE `nothing of these` `no exception` `no such direction` TRUE EQUALS `the investigation` `yes: the death must be investigated (ss 8(c), 19(1))`
#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `another limb` `no exception` `no such direction` FALSE EQUALS `the investigation` (`Will the coroner investigate` `Graham, a fall` `no directions` FALSE)

#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `nothing of these` `no exception` `no such direction` EQUALS `the inquest` `no: the coroner has no jurisdiction, so there can be no inquest`
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` FALSE `held in care` `no exception` `no such direction` EQUALS `the inquest` `yes: an inquest must be held (s 22(1) or s 23(2))`
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `another limb` `no exception` `no such direction` EQUALS `the inquest` `only if the coroner thinks it desirable (s 22(2)); we may ask for one (s 24)`
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `another limb` `no exception` `the Attorney General or the State Coroner has directed an inquest` EQUALS `the inquest` `yes: an inquest must be held (s 22(1) or s 23(2))`
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` FALSE `nothing of these` `no exception` `no such direction` EQUALS `the inquest` (`Must an inquest be held` `Graham, uncertified` `no directions`)

-- s 37(5): Sue, living with him, is first; Chloe, an adult daughter and executor, third; a son of 16 is not on the list; the
-- emergency contact is seventh.
#ASSERT `What is my place in the order of next of kin of the deceased` `as family` `Sue` EQUALS `place` 1
#ASSERT `What is my place in the order of next of kin of the deceased` `as family` `Chloe` EQUALS `place` 3
#ASSERT `What is my place in the order of next of kin of the deceased` `as family` `a son of sixteen` EQUALS `place` 99
#ASSERT `What is my place in the order of next of kin of the deceased` `as family` `the friend` EQUALS `place` 7
#ASSERT `What is my place in the order of next of kin of the deceased` `as family` `the cousin` EQUALS `place` (`What is my place in the order of next of kin` `the cousin`)
#ASSERT `Am I one of the deceased's next of kin` `as family` `Chloe` EQUALS yes
