#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead although I objected` `as family` TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead although I objected` `as family` TRUE 2 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead although I objected` `as family` TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead although I objected` `as family` TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can the post mortem go ahead despite my objection` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May I still ask the Supreme Court to stop the post mortem` `as family` TRUE 1 FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I still ask the Supreme Court to stop the post mortem` `as family` TRUE 2 FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I still ask the Supreme Court to stop the post mortem` `as family` TRUE 3 TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`May I apply to the Supreme Court to stop the post mortem` 3 TRUE)

#ASSERT `Does the coroner hold the body, or may we have it` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `nothing of these` `no exception` FALSE EQUALS `the body` `not held by the coroner: the Coroners Act does not hold it back`
#ASSERT `Does the coroner hold the body, or may we have it` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `another limb` `no exception` FALSE EQUALS `the body` `held by the coroner until the s 29 certificate is issued (s 30(1))`
#ASSERT `Does the coroner hold the body, or may we have it` `as family` `in WA, body here` FALSE `nothing of these` `no exception` TRUE EQUALS `the body` `released: the s 29 certificate permits burial, cremation or other disposal`
#ASSERT `Does the coroner hold the body, or may we have it` `as family` `in WA, body here` FALSE `held in care` `no exception` FALSE EQUALS `the body` (`Does the coroner hold the body` `Graham, lock-up` FALSE)
#ASSERT `When can the coroner issue the certificate releasing the body` `as family` `a request was refused and the 2 clear working days to apply to the Supreme Court are running` EQUALS `the disposal certificate` `not yet: the s 36 application or the time for it must run out first (s 29(2))`
#ASSERT `When can the coroner issue the certificate releasing the body` `as family` `the Supreme Court has ordered a post mortem (s 36(4))` EQUALS `the disposal certificate` `only the State Coroner may issue it, after the ordered post mortem (ss 29(3), 36(4))`
#ASSERT `When can the coroner issue the certificate releasing the body` `as family` `no one's request for a post mortem has been refused` EQUALS `the disposal certificate` `now: the coroner must issue it as soon as reasonably possible (s 29(1))`
#ASSERT `When can the coroner issue the certificate releasing the body` `as family` `the time to apply has passed with no application` EQUALS `the disposal certificate` (`When can the disposal certificate issue` `the time to apply has passed with no application`)

§§ `The death asked in groups: each answer equals the baseline export's on the full record (fixed 6 November 2026)`

-- Fixtures that use the fields and values the Graham fixtures do not, each with its groups (cor-qa.l4, `Building the
-- baseline's inputs`). Several set more than one field of a group, to show that "the first that fits" loses nothing.

`died interstate, the body brought home to WA, certified there, unexpected` MEANS Death WITH
    `occurred in Western Australia` IS FALSE
    `the body is in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `the cause occurred in Western Australia` IS FALSE
    `the deceased ordinarily resided in Western Australia` IS FALSE
    `the deceased was in an industry under the Industrial Relations Act 1979 s 3` IS FALSE
    `appears to have been unexpected` IS TRUE
    `appears to have been unnatural or violent` IS FALSE
    `appears to have resulted, directly or indirectly, from injury` IS FALSE
    `occurred during an anaesthetic` IS FALSE
    `occurred as a result of an anaesthetic and not due to natural causes` IS FALSE
    `the deceased was a person held in care immediately before death` IS FALSE
    `appears caused or contributed to while the deceased was held in care` IS FALSE
    `appears caused or contributed to by an action of a police officer` IS FALSE
    `the identity of the deceased is unknown` IS FALSE
    `a doctor has certified, or will certify, the cause under BDM Act s 44` IS FALSE
    `outside WA, the cause is certified by a legally qualified medical practitioner there` IS TRUE
    `followed a voluntary assisted dying substance under the VAD Act 2019` IS FALSE
    `a child born alive after a lawful abortion, who died following it` IS FALSE

