-- Worked by hand. Interstate, body brought home, certified there but unexpected: a WA death (the body, s 3), reportable
-- (unexpected), and only because unexpected, so with natural causes determined the coroner need not investigate (s 19A).
#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `elsewhere, body here` TRUE `only unexpected` `no exception` `no such direction` TRUE EQUALS `the investigation` `the coroner need not investigate: natural causes, reportable only because unexpected (s 19A)`
-- Interstate, lived in WA, body there, uncertified: reportable by limb (i) for a death outside WA; the coroner does not hold
-- a body outside WA (s 30(1)).
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as family` `elsewhere, another link` FALSE `nothing of these` `no exception` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does the coroner hold the body, or may we have it` `as family` `elsewhere, another link` FALSE `nothing of these` `no exception` FALSE EQUALS `the body` `not held by the coroner: the Coroners Act does not hold it back`
-- Overseas with no link: not a Western Australian death, so not reportable however violent.
#ASSERT `Is this death a Western Australian death` `as a doctor present` `elsewhere, no link` TRUE `another limb` `no exception` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as family` `elsewhere, no link` TRUE `another limb` `no exception` EQUALS no
-- s 3A: VAD is excepted, unless the person was held in care; s 3B: a child after a lawful abortion always.
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `only unexpected` `after VAD` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `held in care` `after VAD` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as family` `in WA, body here` FALSE `held in care` `after a lawful abortion` EQUALS no
-- s 22(1): a death caused by a police officer's action needs an inquest; a body taken out of WA is not held (s 30(1)).
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `care or police` `no exception` `no such direction` EQUALS `the inquest` `yes: an inquest must be held (s 22(1) or s 23(2))`
#ASSERT `Does the coroner hold the body, or may we have it` `as family` `in WA, body gone` TRUE `another limb` `no exception` FALSE EQUALS `the body` `not held by the coroner: the Coroners Act does not hold it back`
-- During an anaesthetic: reportable, and not "only because unexpected", so s 19A does not apply (s 19A(2)).
#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `another limb` `no exception` `no such direction` TRUE EQUALS `the investigation` `yes: the death must be investigated (ss 8(c), 19(1))`

-- The direction, asked as one input: a missing person direction makes the duty by itself (s 23(2)), though Graham's
-- expected death is not reportable and the coroner does not investigate it as one; an Attorney General's direction as
-- the State Coroner's.
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `nothing of these` `no exception` `the State Coroner has directed an investigation of the suspected death of a missing person` EQUALS `the inquest` `yes: an inquest must be held (s 22(1) or s 23(2))`
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `nothing of these` `no exception` `the State Coroner has directed an investigation of the suspected death of a missing person` EQUALS `the inquest` (`Must an inquest be held` `Graham, expected` `a missing person direction`)
#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `nothing of these` `no exception` `the State Coroner has directed an investigation of the suspected death of a missing person` FALSE EQUALS `the investigation` (`Will the coroner investigate` `Graham, expected` `a missing person direction` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `another limb` `no exception` `the Attorney General or the State Coroner has directed an inquest` EQUALS `the inquest` (`Must an inquest be held` `Graham, a fall` `an inquest directed by the Attorney General`)
#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `in WA, body here` TRUE `only unexpected` `no exception` `the Attorney General or the State Coroner has directed an inquest` TRUE EQUALS `the investigation` (`Will the coroner investigate` `Graham, sudden, certified` `an inquest directed by the Attorney General` TRUE)

